{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "None of these items felt like a natural next purchase; the relay at least connects to my past electronics projects, but its specifications do not match my earlier 5V module."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The AC 110/120V relay does not directly fit the low-voltage projects suggested by my Arduino breadboards and 5V relay module; sharing the name 'relay' is not enough.",
    "Wood screws, drywall screws and brad nails assume construction or woodworking needs that my purchases do not establish.",
    "A specific replacement belt and a tap wrench require equipment or tasks I have not shown a need for.",
    "Copper scraps, specialized glue and vibration pads have possible project uses, but I cannot connect them to a current task from my history."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in practical electronics and occasional hardware seems to have been stretched into interest in almost any workshop supply.",
    "My caster purchase seems to have been treated as evidence of broader furniture or machinery work, although it does not establish a need for fasteners or vibration control."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "For electronics parts, voltage, connections and suitability for the same kind of project matter more to me than a shared product name.",
    "My purchases are spread across years and separate tasks; older supplies do not necessarily describe what I am working on now.",
    "I need a specific reason to buy a project supply, especially a large pack or an equipment-specific replacement part."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in practical project supplies but inferred current needs too broadly and missed compatibility and task-specific details."
}"}
